// src/mcp.mind — native `mcp` subcommand (stdio JSON-RPC MCP server).
//
// PURE-MIND PORT (track B, step 1): folds python/mind_nerve/mcp_server.py
// (218 lines) into the mind-nerve single binary as a content-sniffed `mcp`
// mode. cli/main.mind dispatches here when stdin's first byte is `{` (0x7B);
// mic@2 preselect frames start with `m` (0x6D), so the frozen preselect path
// is byte-for-byte unaffected.
//
// PROTOCOL (JSON-RPC 2.0 over line-delimited stdin, matching the Python
// server's shapes):
//   initialize                 -> protocolVersion/serverInfo/capabilities
//   notifications/initialized  -> no reply (notification)
//   tools/list                 -> the single `mind_nerve_route` tool
//   tools/call name=mind_nerve_route args={query,top_k}
//                              -> top-K in-process route ids + Q16.16 scores
//   <anything else>            -> JSON-RPC error -32601
//   <malformed line>           -> JSON-RPC error -32700 (id null)
//
// DoS-HARDENING BY CONSTRUCTION:
//   - stdin is capped at MN_MAX_STDIN_BYTES (64 KiB) by cli/main.mind before
//     a single byte reaches this module.
//   - the JSON scanner is DEPTH-CAPPED (MCP_MAX_JSON_DEPTH) and its value-skip
//     is ITERATIVE (no recursion, so no stack-depth attack) and string-aware
//     (brackets inside strings never move the depth counter).
//   - the query unescape buffer is LENGTH-CAPPED (MCP_QUERY_CAP); an
//     over-long query is rejected as -32602, never a heap blowup.
//
// TWO DELIBERATE LIMITS OF STEP 1 (each flagged for U1 to lift):
//   1. BATCH-ONLY LOOP. src/runtime_ffi.mind's rt_read_stdin loops until the
//      buffer is full OR EOF (see mind/runtime/nerve_rt_shims.c) — it cannot
//      return one line at a time, so a LIVE interactive client that waits for
//      each response before sending the next would block. This module
//      therefore processes a whole buffered batch (all newline-delimited
//      messages up to EOF), which is exactly what the golden-transcript replay
//      and any client that half-closes stdin need. A live interactive server
//      needs a NEW streaming shim (rt_read_line / rt_read_avail) — flagged.
//   2. tools/call ROUTE PATH is fully wired (tokenize -> load -> infer ->
//      format) in mcp_route_compute, but model/catalog paths cannot be
//      resolved without a getenv/argv shim (none exists — adding an extern
//      would break the native link and fail the compile gate). Until that
//      shim lands, MN_MCP_PATHS_READY stays 0 and tools/call FAILS CLOSED with
//      an explicit `unavailable` payload (mirrors the Python daemon-down
//      branch). No machine-specific path is baked into the OSS binary.
//
// NATIVE-vs-PYTHON SEMANTICS (intentional divergence — see the gate spec in
// tests/harness/mcp_golden.sh): the native tool ranks IN-PROCESS with the
// deterministic Q16.16 preselector, so its `tools/list` description carries no
// daemon/fail-closed/Windows-fallback language, and `tools/call` returns route
// *ids* (32-byte SHA-256, hex) with fixed-point scores rather than the
// daemon's route metadata. The JSON-RPC framing, protocolVersion, error codes,
// and id-echo ARE identical to Python and are the byte-compared subset.

import src.lib;
import src.runtime_ffi;
import src.tokenizer;
import src.loader;
import src.inference;
import mind.luts.exp_q16;
import mind.luts.sqrt_q16;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Tunables
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

const MCP_MAX_JSON_DEPTH: i64 = 32;
const MCP_QUERY_CAP:      i64 = 8192;   // unescaped query bytes; > => -32602
const MCP_RESP_CAP:       i64 = 16384;  // per-response scratch (64 routes fit)
// Max bytes of the request `id` token echoed verbatim into a MCP_RESP_CAP
// response buffer. The id is copied byte-for-byte by mcp_put_id, so an
// uncapped id (attacker sends {"id":<40000 digits>,...}, which fits the 64 KiB
// stdin cap) would overrun the 16 KiB response buffer. 512 >> any real
// JSON-RPC client id (ints, uuids); an over-long id echoes null (see
// mcp_handle_line). Mirrors the MCP_QUERY_CAP guard on the sibling query field.
const MCP_ID_CAP:         i64 = 512;
const MCP_DEFAULT_TOP_K:  i64 = 5;
const MCP_PATH_CAP:       i64 = 4096;   // constructed bundle-path byte cap

// WIRED (2026-08-17): tools/call resolves the model + catalog bundle from
// $MIND_NERVE_RUNTIME_DIR via rt_getenv (src/runtime_ffi.mind) and ranks
// in-process. Still FAILS CLOSED (explicit `unavailable` payload, never a
// crash, no baked path) when the env var is unset (rt_getenv => -2) or the
// bundle is absent / not the native MNC1/MNW1 format the loader requires.
const MN_MCP_PATHS_READY: i64 = 1;

// JSON-RPC error codes (match the Python server).
const MCP_ERR_PARSE:      i64 = -32700;
const MCP_ERR_METHOD:     i64 = -32601;
const MCP_ERR_PARAMS:     i64 = -32602;

